From: =?UTF-8?q?Ren=C3=AA=20de=20Souza=20Pinto?= <rene@renesp.com.br>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:10:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Add named gptprio GPT attribute fields
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GPT attribute bits 48-63 are partition-type specific. The existing named
A/B fields (priority, tries-remaining, active, successful, unbootable)
follow the qbootctl layout, while GRUB's gptprio module (gptprio.next),
using a bit layout that comes from ChromeOS, puts priority at bits 48-51,
tries left at 52-55 and successful at bit 56. The names clash and the
bits overlap, so e.g. successful sets bit 54, which gptprio reads as
tries left.

Add scheme-prefixed YAML fields for gptprio instead of requiring raw
attributes hex: gptprio-priority, gptprio-tries-left and
gptprio-successful.

They are passed through partitions.xml as gptprio_* and written to the
GPT entry, replacing any raw attributes bits they cover, so a named
field wins over attributes as it does for the other fields. A
partition that sets bits through both qbootctl and gptprio fields is
rejected.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Renê de Souza Pinto <rene@renesp.com.br>
